# Personal Codex routing overlay

This owner-private layer-3 file is selected only by an explicit
`setup-codex.sh --personal-layer <this-layer>` invocation. It enters the local
layer-4 global composite; never copy it into a shared or public repository.

## Personal-source routing

When a task requires owner-specific preferences, identity, account handling,
cross-repository state, or an operational rule, locate this layer from the
generated header. Search its `CLAUDE.md` index, then read only the relevant
linked source before acting.

Keep only trigger + imperative read pointer stubs here. A bare Markdown link is
not transcluded, while copied rule bodies create a second source of truth.
Detailed rules stay in their owning files and current state stays in the
relevant repository's `SESSION.md`. Contract:
the `claude-config` repository's
`codex/PARITY.md#instruction-entrypoint-kernel`, located through the generated
`public-source` header.
